  "summary": "Tetris 99 is Arika's online puzzle game, released for Nintendo Switch Online members on 13 February 2019.",
  "body": [
    "Tetris 99 is Arika's online puzzle game, released for Nintendo Switch Online members on 13 February 2019. Ninety-nine people play Tetris simultaneously, each trying to remain after every other board has overflowed. Rotating and arranging tetrominoes still clears complete horizontal lines, but successful combinations also send garbage rows to opponents. The player's own well occupies the centre of a screen filled with smaller rival boards, making a solitary-looking puzzle part of a contest whose pressure can arrive from several directions.",
    "Targeting adds another decision to placing the falling pieces. The player can select an individual opponent or use automatic strategies that seek vulnerable players, attack rivals with badges or retaliate against attackers. Clearing lines can cancel incoming garbage before it enters the well. A useful move may therefore provide breathing room instead of immediately damaging someone else. Tetrises, T-spins and consecutive clears reward the ability to build an attack while preserving space for the next unexpected delivery.",
    "Knocking out an opponent awards badge pieces and transfers the defeated player's collected badges, increasing the strength of later attacks. A successful competitor gradually becomes more dangerous and more tempting to target. The pace also rises as fewer players remain, turning careful early construction into a test of rapid decisions. Later additions included offline modes and team battles. The original online format gives every cleared row two meanings: space recovered on the player's board and pressure potentially passed to another person."
  ],
  "story_headings": [
    "A familiar well among ninety-eight rivals",
    "Choose where the cleared lines go",
    "Survive long enough to become the target"
  ],
